{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Retimed target-misalign trap\n\nChanged the EX1/EX2 payload so it no longer carries `branch_misalign` or\n`jump_misalign`. EX1 still registers `branch_cond`, `branch_target`, and\n`jump_target`; EX2 now computes `misalign_fault` from those registered values:\ntaken misaligned branches trap, jumps with misaligned resolved targets trap,\nand not-taken misaligned conditional branches do not trap.\n\nMirrored the payload cleanup in `00_core_pkg.sv`. Added a focused cocotb case\nfor a not-taken conditional branch whose target would be misaligned, alongside\nthe existing taken-branch/JAL/JALR misalignment tests.\n\nNo deliberate deviations from the hypothesis. One local tooling note: plain\n`make cosim TARGET=bench` compiled the harness with its default `NRET=2` and\nfailed before simulation because this core declares `nret: 1`; rerunning with\n`NRET=1` matches the declared port set and passed.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_branch_retime.py`: pass\n- `TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the retimed target-misalign trap.\n\nChanged:\n- Removed `branch_misalign` / `jump_misalign` from EX1/EX2 payload in [`core_pkg.sv`](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261004-001-r11s0/cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv) and [`00_core_pkg.sv`](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261004-001-r11s0/cores/bench/rtl/00_core_pkg.sv).\n- Recomputed `misalign_fault` in EX2 from registered `branch_cond`, `branch_target`, `jump_target`, and control bits in [`ex_stage.sv`](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261004-001-r11s0/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv).\n- Added a not-taken misaligned conditional branch regression in [`test_branch_retime.py`](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261004-001-r11s0/cores/bench/test/test_branch_retime.py).\n- Wrote [`implementation_notes.md`](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261004-001-r11s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md).\n\nChecks:\n- Verilator lint: pass\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_branch_retime.py`: pass\n- Formal: pass, `53 passed, 0 failed`\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested\n\nNote: plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` failed before simulation because the local Makefile defaulted the harness to `NRET=2`, while this core declares `nret: 1`."}}
