{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,150p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Decouple ID operand refresh\n\nChanged:\n- Removed the stall-controlled regfile read-address mux from id_stage. The\n  read ports now always use the currently fetched instruction's rs1/rs2 fields.\n- Added WB-stage write enable/address/data inputs to id_stage. While ID/EX is\n  stalled, only held operands whose source register matches the WB writeback\n  address are refreshed from wb_w_data; all other ID/EX fields stay held.\n- Split the forwarding lookahead source addresses in core.sv from the regfile\n  read addresses. Forwarding still tracks the held ID/EX instruction during\n  stalls, but the regfile read cone no longer depends on the broad stall signal.\n- Added a pipeline cocotb case where a consumer is held in ID/EX by DIV while\n  an older producer writes back, proving the direct WB refresh keeps the\n  consumer operand fresh.\n\nDeviations:\n- None from the hypothesis intent. I kept the forwarding retargeting logic in\n  core.sv because the existing forward_unit uses the same source-address wires\n  for lookahead bookkeeping; leaving it tied to the regfile read ports would\n  make held-stall forwarding observe the wrong instruction.\n\nConcerns:\n- The plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` target runs its `cosim-build` prerequisite\n  with the build script's default NRET=2 before the Python evaluator can inject\n  the nret value from core.yaml. This core is nret=1, so that exact command\n  fails at C++ compile time looking for channel-1 RVFI ports. Running the same\n  gate with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` matches the declared core contract.\n\nLocal status:\n- Verilator lint: pass\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py`: pass\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass\n  (53 passed, 0 failed)\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench`: fails before simulation due the NRET=2 Makefile\n  prerequisite mismatch described above\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass (`{\"passed\": true, \"elfs_tested\": 2}`)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
