{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the ID operand refresh decoupling.\n\nChanged:\n- `id_stage.sv`: regfile read addresses now always come from the fetched instruction; held operands refresh directly from WB on matching source register.\n- `core.sv`: wired WB into ID and split forwarding lookahead source addresses from regfile read addresses.\n- `test_pipeline.py`: added divider-stall coverage for a held ID/EX consumer refreshed from WB.\n\nChecks:\n- `verilator --lint-only ...`: pass\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py`: pass\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53/53\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass\n\nNote: plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` fails before simulation because its Makefile prerequisite builds with default `NRET=2` while this core is declared `nret: 1`; documented in `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`."}}
