{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"The key correctness wrinkle is forwarding: the held divide can’t look like a fresh EX1 producer after its result is already buffered. I’m keeping the stall output registered, but delaying the EX/MEM emit by one cycle so the existing forwarding predictor sees a normal “EX1 advances to EX/MEM” event."}}
