{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Resetless LUTRAM register file\n\nChanged `rtl/reg_file.sv` from a synchronously reset 32x32 register array to a resetless array:\n\n- Removed the full-register reset loop from the write clocked process.\n- Kept x0 hardwired to zero and kept writes to x0 suppressed.\n- Preserved the same-cycle write-first read bypass on both read ports.\n- Added an initial zero fill for simulation and FPGA bitstream power-up flows that honor memory initialization.\n- Added distributed/LUTRAM-style inference attributes (`ram_style = \"distributed\"`, `syn_ramstyle = \"distributed_ram\"`).\n- Left the `reset` port on the module for top-level interface compatibility, but it is intentionally unused by the array storage.\n\nUpdated `test/test_reg_file.py` rather than adding a separate resetless test file. The directed coverage now checks reset release/initial zero values, verifies that a written nonzero register survives a reset pulse, and retains coverage for x0 behavior, ordinary writes, two read ports, and write-first bypass.\n\nNo pipeline, forwarding, divider, memory, RVFI, or top-level IO behavior was changed.\n\nConcerns:\n\n- The LUTRAM attribute names are best-effort hints across FPGA tools. Verilator and formal accept them; final Gowin inference quality still depends on the vendor synthesizer.\n- Plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` in this checkout defaults the C++ harness to `NRET=2`, while `cores/bench/core.yaml` declares `nret: 1`. I reran cosim with `NRET=1`, matching the core contract and the formal wrapper selection.\n\nLocal status:\n\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
