{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"The failure is now clear: a load into `x9` retires, then an `AUIPC` whose immediate bits contain `rs2 == x9` no longer stalls. That is architecturally fine for the instruction itself, but the existing reg-check trace shows the prior broad stall was also covering a load writeback timing hole after a one-cycle spacing case. I’m checking whether this is a formal-only artifact from `rvfi_rd_addr` not gated by `valid`, or a real regfile update mismatch."}}
