{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"The trace is interesting: the failing store reads x18 after an older aligned load wrote x18, but there is also an intervening misaligned load to x18 in EX/MEM that traps and does not write. Letting the store pass that trapping EX/MEM load made it miss the older x18 value. I’m adding a narrow exception: store rs2 may pass EX/MEM loads only when that load’s data will actually write back; misaligned loads still create the one-cycle refresh stall."}}
