{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Retimed two-stage execute path\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added an `ex1_ex2_t` pipeline bundle in `core_pkg.sv` and the alphabetical `00_core_pkg.sv` shim.\n- Reworked `ex_stage.sv` into EX1 operand forwarding/selection plus an EX1/EX2 register feeding EX2 ALU, branch/jump, memory-address, misalignment, and divider completion logic.\n- Added current-EX2 result forwarding, while retaining EX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding. Loads are not forwarded from EX2 or EX/MEM as data.\n- Updated load-use hazard detection to account for loads in both ID/EX and EX1/EX2.\n- Wired the new EX2 metadata through `core.sv`.\n- Updated `test_pipeline.py` to include `iter_divider.sv` in the pipeline test source list.\n\nDeviations:\n- Kept the public `ex_stage` module boundary instead of splitting into new modules.\n- Added same-cycle EX2-to-EX1 bypassing to avoid adding bubbles to normal back-to-back ALU dependencies. This leaves an ALU-to-forward-mux path, but cuts the original regfile/forward-select/ALU cone.\n\nConcerns:\n- Taken branches and jumps now resolve from EX2, so the intended extra control-flow penalty is present.\n- The generic `make cosim TARGET=bench` target invokes the harness with default `NRET=2`; this pre-existing Makefile/build-script default does not match `cores/bench/core.yaml` (`nret: 1`). The matching run with `NRET=1` passes.\n- Timing was not run locally.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELF tests.\n- `make test TARGET=bench`: pass, 6 tests.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
