{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"BRAM-safe store skid LSU\n\nChanged `mem_stage.sv` so all stores first enter a single registered\nstore-request record. That record is the only source that drives\n`io_dmemAddr`, `io_dmemWData`, and `io_dmemWEn` for writes. Ordinary RAM\nstores retire when they enqueue into an empty slot, or when they replace a\nslot that is handshaking in the same cycle. Loads, misaligned memory traps,\nFENCE/SYSTEM, and MMIO stores wait for the slot to empty.\n\nMMIO stores also use the registered request record, but they do not retire\nuntil their write has handshaken with `io_dmemReady`. This keeps marker/UART\nstores precise while avoiding a replay/live write priority mux on the dmem\nwrite port.\n\nChanged `hazard_unit.sv` and `core.sv` so MEM provides `lsu_stall`; the\nhazard unit no longer freezes the pipeline from raw `!io_dmemReady`.\nOrdinary RAM stores can therefore retire into the skid slot while younger\nnon-memory instructions continue behind a pending dmem write.\n\nAlso fixed `test_pipeline.py`'s Verilator source list to include\n`iter_divider.sv`, which `ex_stage.sv` instantiates.\n\nDeviations:\n- I did not add new package fields; ordered operations are identified in\n  MEM from the opcode bits, which kept the pipeline bundles unchanged.\n- MMIO stores are registered for one cycle before the external write, then\n  retire only on the write handshake. This preserves the single registered\n  dmem write source at the cost of one untimed marker setup cycle.\n\nConcerns:\n- RAM stores retire before the physical dmem write drains, so correctness\n  depends on the MEM-stage rule that all later loads, stores, and ordered\n  instructions wait for the slot. ALU/control instructions may retire while\n  the store drains.\n\nLocal status:\n- Verilator lint: pass\n- Cocotb pipeline smoke: pass\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed\n- Cosim: pass with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`; plain `make cosim\n  TARGET=bench` hit the repository Makefile/build default of `NRET=2` before\n  simulation, which mismatches this core's declared `nret: 1` port set.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
