{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Retimed redirect squash path\n\nChanged RTL:\n- Removed EX redirect from hazard_unit's ID/EX flush decision. The hazard\n  unit now only flushes ID/EX for load-use bubbles and only requests IF NOPs\n  for imem stalls; redirect NOP emission remains local to if_stage.\n- Added squash_ex_q in core.sv. It is updated with the same hold/flush\n  discipline as the ID/EX register: clear on reset/load-use flush, hold during\n  dmem/divider stalls, and arm from redirect only when ID/EX advances.\n- Added a squash input to ex_stage. A squashed or otherwise invalid ID/EX\n  payload is converted to an inactive bubble by zeroing effective control,\n  suppressing redirects, divider starts/holds, memory requests, traps, and\n  register writes.\n- Gated the load-use hazard input with ID/EX valid and !squash_ex_q so a\n  squashed raw load encoding cannot create a false dependency stall.\n\nTests:\n- Added test_redirect_squash.py with cocotb coverage for taken branches and\n  JALs under imem stalls, dmem stalls behind an older load, and skipped DIV\n  slots that would expose an unsuppressed wrong-path divider operation.\n- Added iter_divider.sv to the cocotb source lists used by the new regression\n  and the existing pipeline regression.\n\nDeviations / concerns:\n- if_stage still emits a NOP on redirect, as requested. In this particular\n  core there is no separate IF/ID flop, so that NOP means the squash bit is\n  often aligned with a bubble rather than a real wrong-path instruction. The\n  structural feedback removal is still present: redirect no longer drives the\n  hazard_unit -> id_stage flush path.\n\nLocal status:\n- verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv: pass\n- python -m pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_redirect_squash.py: pass\n- python -m pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py: pass\n- RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed\n- make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1: pass, 2 ELF files tested\n- make cosim TARGET=bench without NRET=1 failed before RTL execution because test/cosim/build.sh defaults NRET=2 while cores/bench/core.yaml declares nret: 1.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
