{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Valid-only frontend squash implementation\n\nChanged:\n- `if_stage.sv` now leaves `out.instr` equal to raw `imem_data` on flush or redirect and only clears `out.valid`.\n- `id_stage.sv` latches a zeroed ID/EX bubble whenever IF/ID `valid` is low and the stage is not otherwise held. Regfile read addresses still come from raw instruction bits, or from the held ID/EX instruction during stalls.\n- `mem_stage.sv` gates dmem read/write enables, RVFI memory masks, and MEM/WB control propagation with the EX/MEM valid bit so invalid bubbles cannot issue memory side effects.\n- Comments in `core.sv`, `if_stage.sv`, and `hazard_unit.sv` were updated to describe invalid squashes instead of squash-to-NOP.\n- Added `test_valid_squash.py` with branch-redirect and imem-stall cases where invalid raw bits decode as writer/load/store instructions.\n\nDeviations:\n- No new predictor, target logic, replay buffer, or RAM-port muxing was added.\n- I kept the existing redirect priority and stall policy unchanged.\n\nConcerns:\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` in this checkout invokes the cosim build with the build script's default `NRET=2`, which does not match `cores/bench/core.yaml` (`nret: 1`). The orchestrator path documents and supplies `NRET=1`; using that setting, cosim passes.\n\nLocal checks:\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed, run as `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`.\n- Focused cocotb test: pass, `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_valid_squash.py`.\n- Cosim: initial bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` failed during C++ compile due the NRET mismatch above; rerun as `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed with 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
