{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_70", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,120p' formal/checks.cfg && sed -n '1,80p' formal/checks_si.cfg && rg -n \\\"RISCV_FORMAL\\\" formal/checks*.cfg formal/wrapper*.sv\"", "aggregated_output": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 2\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Substitutes M-ext mul/div/rem with\n# simpler XOR-of-add/sub formulas so bitwuzla solves them inside the\n# 20-step BMC budget (rvfi.rst §7.6 \"Alternative arithmetic operations\").\n#\n# IMPORTANT — what this DOES and DOES NOT prove:\n#   ✓ proves: M-ext bypassing, operand routing (rs1/rs2 -> unit -> rd),\n#             stall/forwarding behavior on mul/div, all I-base arithmetic\n#             and trap discipline.\n#   ✗ does NOT prove: the actual MUL/DIV/REM arithmetic is correct.\n#     The DUT and the spec both implement the same XOR substitute under\n#     this define, so a wrong real multiplier can still pass formal here.\n#\n# M-extension arithmetic correctness is covered separately by:\n#   1. test/test_alu.py — 30+ vectors per M-ext op, exact bit results.\n#   2. cosim against test/cosim/reference.py — every retired MUL/DIV/REM\n#      diff'd field-by-field.\n#   3. `make formal-deep` — same checks without ALTOPS. SLOW (~hours per\n#      M-ext check) but proves real arithmetic. Run periodically, not in\n#      the per-iteration orchestrator loop.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\n# A vacuous suite (nothing ever retires) would fail this — no symbolic\n# trace can make rvfi_val\n…[1562 of 4634 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f03caec0b8b40dc5]…\n.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\nformal/checks.cfg:25:`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\nformal/checks.cfg:26:# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Substitutes M-ext mul/div/rem with\nformal/checks.cfg:45:`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\nformal/checks_si.cfg:25:`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\nformal/checks_si.cfg:26:# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\nformal/checks_si.cfg:29:`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\nformal/checks-deep.cfg:25:`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\nformal/checks-deep.cfg:26:# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Substitutes M-ext mul/div/rem with\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
