{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_89","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"ls -l cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench3 hwebench3 2448 Oct  4 07:08 cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\nDecoded operand-use predictor implementation notes\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added rs1_used and rs2_used to ctrl_t in core_pkg.sv and the alphabetical\n  00_core_pkg.sv shim.\n- decoder.sv now marks exact legal RV32IM source usage:\n  R/M, STORE, and BRANCH use both; OP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR use rs1; LUI,\n  AUIPC, JAL, FENCE, EBREAK, and illegal/default encodings use neither.\n- id_stage.sv latches the source-use bits with ID/EX and exposes the\n  next-instruction source-use qualifiers alongside the existing read addresses.\n- hazard_unit.sv gates EX1 and EX/MEM-load RAW interlocks with the decoded\n  source-use bits.\n- forward_unit.sv forces FWD_NONE for unused operands by gating its tag\n  matching with next-instruction source-use qualifiers.\n- core.sv wires the new qualifiers through ID, hazard, and forwarding.\n- core.sv also keeps raw RVFI source addresses for non-formal cosim, using an\n  RVFI-only commit shadow register file to report correct raw source data for\n  unused encoded fields without reintroducing execution stalls. In formal,\n  unused RVFI source addresses/data are zeroed under RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n  to keep the riscv-formal state space small.\n- Added test/test_source_use_predictor.py with focused decoder, hazard, and\n  forwarding tests for false and true source-use cases.\n\nDeviations:\n- The RVFI reporting needed extra care beyond the original hazard/forwarding\n  plan. Cosim expects raw encoded rs1/rs2 addresses and data for every\n  instruction, while riscv-formal accepts zeroed unused sources and otherwise\n  requires reported data to be architecturally fresh. The implementation keeps\n  the execution optimization and handles those verification views separately.\n\nConcerns:\n- The non-formal RVFI shadow is verification-only and should be pruned from\n  timed FPGA logic because it only feeds RVFI outputs, but it is still present\n  in simulation builds.\n- Plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` in this checkout invokes build.sh with its\n  default NRET=2 before tools.eval.cosim can inject core.yaml's nret value.\n  The matching local command is `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_source_use_predictor.py`: pass, 3 passed.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed and 0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
