{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"A couple of correctness details matter here: EX needs to compare the predicted next PC against the resolved next PC for every valid instruction, not only branches, so any stale or aliased BTB hit is recoverable. Predictor updates will be gated to the cycle the EX instruction can actually advance, which avoids repeatedly training on an instruction held behind a memory stall."}}
