{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Static backward direct predictor implementation notes\n\nChanged:\n- Added a single `pred_taken` bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles in both\n  `core_pkg.sv` and the alphabetic-build shim `00_core_pkg.sv`.\n- Added IF-side static direct-control predecode in `if_stage.sv`.\n  Conditional branches with valid branch funct3, negative B-immediate sign,\n  and aligned in-range direct target predict taken. Direct JAL with an aligned\n  in-range target predicts taken. Other instructions continue to fetch `pc+4`.\n- Latched the prediction bit through `id_stage.sv`.\n- Reworked `ex_stage.sv` redirect generation so redirect now means recovery:\n  correctly predicted taken direct branches/JALs do not flush, untaken exits\n  from predicted branches redirect to `pc+4`, and unpredicted taken branches,\n  JALR, and unpredicted JAL still redirect to the resolved target.\n\nDeviations:\n- I gated IF prediction on the direct target being word-aligned. Misaligned\n  taken branch/JAL still traps and retires with `pc+4`, so predicting those\n  targets would only create an avoidable recovery case.\n- I also gated prediction on the direct target being inside the 1 MiB memory\n  range observed by the cosim harness, because speculative fetch addresses are\n  externally visible and should not create false OOB failures.\n- I also checked branch funct3 in IF so reserved branch encodings are not\n  speculated as real conditional branches.\n\nConcerns:\n- This keeps the predictor zero-state, but it does put direct immediate\n  formation and a target mux on the IF PC-update path. Prior learned predictors\n  regressed Fmax through fetch-path cost, so the FPGA result is the real arbiter.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested. A plain\n  `make cosim TARGET=bench` in this checkout defaulted the cosim CFLAGS to\n  `NRET=2` and failed at C++ compile time looking for channel-1 RVFI ports;\n  the explicit `NRET=1` matches `cores/bench/core.yaml` and the formal run.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the static backward direct predictor in `cores/bench/rtl/`:\n\n- IF predicts aligned, in-range backward conditional branches and direct JALs.\n- `pred_taken` is carried through IF/ID and ID/EX.\n- EX now redirects only for prediction recovery, while preserving JALR, illegal, and misalignment behavior.\n- Notes written to `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`.\n\nVerification:\n- `verilator --lint-only ...`: pass\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53/53\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested\n\nOne local wrinkle: plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` defaulted the cosim build to `NRET=2` in this checkout and failed before simulation looking for channel-1 RVFI ports. `NRET=1` matches `cores/bench/core.yaml` and the formal path."}}
