{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Tiny return-stack predictor implementation notes\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added `rtl/return_stack.sv`, a 4-entry registered return-address stack.\n  Pushes keep the newest four return addresses; pops on an empty stack are\n  ignored.\n- Added `pred_return` and `pred_target` metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX\n  bundles in both `core_pkg.sv` and the alphabetic `00_core_pkg.sv` shim.\n- Updated IF to recognize only exact canonical return encodings\n  `jalr x0, 0(x1)` and `jalr x0, 0(x5)`. When the RAS is non-empty, IF uses\n  the registered top entry as the next PC and emits prediction metadata.\n- Updated EX to push link-register calls (`rd` x1/x5), pop real canonical\n  returns, suppress the normal JALR redirect for correct return predictions,\n  and redirect to the resolved next PC on RAS mispredicts.\n- Wired the RAS in `core.sv` between EX update signals and IF prediction\n  inputs. The top-level IO contract is unchanged.\n\nDeviations:\n- RAS push/pop pulses are gated with `!stall` so a jump held behind an older\n  dmem stall does not update the stack repeatedly while EX keeps presenting\n  the same instruction.\n- Misaligned jump/return traps do not update the RAS. A predicted return that\n  resolves as misaligned redirects back to `pc+4` to recover the wrong-path\n  fetch.\n\nConcerns:\n- The stack is intentionally tiny and purely speculative. Deep call nesting\n  beyond four entries drops the oldest address, so older returns may still\n  mispredict.\n- IF still compares the full fetched instruction against two constants on the\n  fetch path. This is much smaller than a BTB/BHT path but is not free.\n\nLocal verification:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`\n  passed.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` passed:\n  53 passed, 0 failed.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` failed before simulation because the Makefile\n  build path defaulted the harness to `NRET=2` while `cores/bench/core.yaml`\n  declares `nret: 1`.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed: 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
