{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r10s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r10s0\ntitle: \"Retimed divider result postprocess\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's worst path has moved inside `cpu/u_ex/u_divider`, from\n  `dividend_q[31]` to `result_q`. That points at the final divider iteration:\n  the last shift/compare/subtract feeds quotient or remainder selection and\n  signed two's-complement post-processing before reaching the result register.\n\n  DIV/REM are cold for CoreMark compared with ADD, load/store address, branch,\n  and MUL traffic. A local divider retime can therefore trade one extra cycle on\n  rare divide/remainder instructions for a cleaner global Fmax without touching\n  the hot execute, frontend, LSU, or memory wrapper paths that prior attempts\n  made fragile.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a registered divider post-processing stage. On the final restoring divide\n  step, latch the raw quotient and raw remainder plus the saved sign-control\n  bits, then compute the signed quotient/remainder result from those registered\n  values in the following cycle before asserting `valid`.\n\n  This removes the final subtract/compare result from the same cycle as the\n  quotient/remainder select and 32-bit two's-complement correction. Ordinary\n  divides become roughly one cycle longer, while divide-by-zero and signed\n  overflow special cases can keep their current fast completion. Since CoreMark\n  is not division-heavy and the current worst path is divider-only, the expected\n  net effect is a higher median FPGA Fmax with negligible IPC loss.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/iter_divider.sv\n    description: \"Insert a registered postprocess state that captures raw quotient/remainder at the final divide step, applies sign correction from registered values one cycle later, and keeps the existing start/valid/consume contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Keep or extend RV32M DIV/REM vectors around sign, divide-by-zero, and INT_MIN/-1 cases so the extra divider postprocess state preserves exact architectural results.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
