{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r11s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r11s0\ntitle: \"Retimed target-misalign trap\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's reported worst path ends at `cpu/u_ex/ex1_q.branch_misalign_s0`\n  after passing through `cpu/u_fwd` and `cpu/u_ex`. That means the EX1 register is\n  still asking the forwarded operand compare path to also produce the rare\n  instruction-address-misaligned trap bit for taken branches.\n\n  Target misalignment is correctness-critical but cold on CoreMark's legal code,\n  and the existing two-stage execute path already registers `branch_cond`,\n  `branch_target`, and `jump_target` before EX2 redirect/trap selection. The trap\n  bit does not need to be precomputed in EX1 from the live forwarding cone.\nhypothesis: |\n  Stop carrying `branch_misalign` and `jump_misalign` as EX1-computed payload\n  fields. Instead, register only the existing branch condition and branch/jump\n  targets in EX1/EX2, then compute `misalign_fault` locally in EX2 from those\n  registered values:\n  taken branch and `branch_target[1:0] != 0`, or jump and `jump_target[1:0] != 0`.\n\n  This preserves precise RVFI trap behavior for misaligned taken branches and\n  jumps, keeps redirect suppression in the same architectural stage, and adds no\n  CoreMark IPC penalty. It should shorten the current Fmax limiter by removing\n  one destination and an extra target-low-bit gate from the forwarded\n  rs1/rs2-to-EX1 register path, while avoiding the predictor and LSU changes that\n  repeatedly regressed in prior rounds.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Remove branch_misalign and jump_misalign from the EX1/EX2 payload, or leave them unused while no longer driving them from EX1 combinational forwarding paths.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the EX1/EX2 payload cleanup in the alphabetical build-order shim.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute misalign_fault in EX2 from registered branch_cond, branch_target, jump_target, and control bits instead of latching branch_misalign/jump_misalign in EX1.\"\n  - file: test/test_target_misalign.py\n    description: \"Add focused branch/JALR misaligned-target tests, including not-taken misaligned conditional branches, to protect the retimed trap behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
