{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r12s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r12s0\ntitle: \"Decouple ID operand refresh\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's worst path starts at `ex1_q.ctrl.alu_op[4]`, passes through divider/execute stall control, and reaches ID/regfile logic. This suggests the broad ID-stage stall signal is still pulling rare divider-control fanout into the combinational register-file read path. The present ID stage uses `stall` to switch read addresses back to the held ID/EX instruction so long stalls can refresh stale operands after writeback; that safety mechanism is useful, but the read-address mux does not need to be driven by every divider, dmem, and RAW stall.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the ID/EX hold semantics, but remove the `stall ? reg_q.rs*_addr : in.instr[...]` mux from the regfile read ports. Drive `rs1_addr` and `rs2_addr` from the currently fetched instruction unconditionally, and during a held ID/EX cycle update only the latched `rs1_val`/`rs2_val` whose held source register matches the WB-stage writeback address, using `wb_w_data` directly. All other held fields and operands remain unchanged.\n\n  This preserves the reason the old stalled-read-address path existed: an instruction held for a long dmem/divider/RAW stall still observes an older producer when it writes back. The difference is that the divider/global-stall signal no longer selects the regfile read address or fans into the distributed-RAM read cone. Forwarding tags continue to cover EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypass cases, so CoreMark IPC should be unchanged while the current `u_ex/u_divider -> u_id -> u_rf` timing path shortens.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Remove the stall-controlled regfile read-address mux; add WB writeback inputs and refresh held ID/EX operand values directly on matching stalled writes while otherwise holding operands stable.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the existing WB-stage write enable, address, and data signals into id_stage so stalled operand refresh no longer depends on retargeting the regfile read ports.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add or extend stall/forwarding coverage for a held ID/EX consumer whose producer writes back during divider or memory backpressure, confirming direct WB refresh preserves correctness.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
