 behavior for misaligned taken branches and\\njumps, keeps redirect suppression in the same architectural stage, and adds no\\nCoreMark IPC penalty. It should shorten the current Fmax limiter by removing\\none destination and an extra target-low-bit gate from the forwarded\\nrs1/rs2-t\n…[21341 of 24413 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c063a9aac5ac1045]…\nstage so held operands can be refreshed without using stall-controlled regfile read addresses.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_id_operand_hold.py\", \"description\": \"Cover a held ID/EX instruction with one source updated by WB while another dependency or dmem/divider stall keeps the instruction from advancing.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 156.93, \"delta_pct\": -6.61, \"vs_baseline\": 1194.8, \"fmax_mhz\": 85.499, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 5448155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2866, \"ff\": 945, \"seeds\": [84.44, 85.499, 85.499], \"perturbations\": [[0, 84.44, 13], [1, 85.499, 14], [2, 85.499, 14]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/ex1_q.branch_misalign_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.843, \"arrival_ns\": 17.137, \"logic_cells\": 37, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T05:07:27.648317Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 12}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
