{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"branch_misalign|jump_misalign|mul_|ALU_MUL|shifted|byte_mask|mem_misalign|pc_next|fwd_w_en|ctrl_with_trap\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md'", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:14:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-001-r5s0\", \"title\": \"Single shared multiplier datapath\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current champion is still timing through the ID/EX operand path and the EX-stage ALU, while prior attempts that added new add/address selectors or frontend prediction lost Fmax. The remaining ALU cone still builds three independent real RV32M multiply products every cycle and then selects among their low/high halves in the same result mux used by hot ADD/address operations. CoreMark needs one-cycle multiply throughput, but it does not need three parallel multiplier trees.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current champion is still timing through the ID/EX operand path and the EX-stage ALU, while prior attempts that added new add/address selectors or frontend prediction lost Fmax. The remaining ALU cone still builds three independent real RV32M multiply products every cycle and then selects among their low/high halves in the same result mux used by hot ADD/address operations. CoreMark needs one-cycle multiply throughput, but it does not need three parallel multiplier trees.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the three parallel multiplier expressions in rtl/alu.sv with one shared 33x33 signed product whose operand sign bits are selected from the decoded MUL variant. MUL can use the low 32 bits, while MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU use bits 63:32 of the same mathematical product after choosing signed/signed, unsigned/unsigned, or signed/unsigned operand extension. Keep DIV/REM in the existing iterative divider and leave the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutes unchanged.\\n\\nThis should preserve CoreMark's cycle count and the successful one-cycle MUL behavior while reducing DSP/LUT use, multiplier output fan-in, and routing load on the ALU result mux. Because it removes redundant arithmetic rather than adding a new post-adder selector, it targets the current timing lesson more directly than the failed fast-address and dedicated-address experiments.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fit\n…[45503 of 48575 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ab1025c07df065d6]…\negression\", \"fitness\": 153.23, \"delta_pct\": -8.81, \"vs_baseline\": 1164.27, \"fmax_mhz\": 83.483, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 5448155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2686, \"ff\": 880, \"seeds\": [86.617, 83.483, 83.483], \"perturbations\": [[0, 86.617, 13], [1, 83.483, 13], [2, 83.483, 13]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/ex1_q.branch_misalign_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.545, \"arrival_ns\": 16.839, \"logic_cells\": 38, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T05:20:29.994840Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-002-r13s1 (regression, -8.81%): Registering only the DIV/REM front-end hold can regress when live `div_valid`/`div_ex_hold` still drives forwarding `ex1_advances`, because the remaining divider feedback plus extra capture/load bookkeeping and cold bubble outweigh isolating IF/ID stall.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
