{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r6s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Iterative cold high-multiply unit\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion still times through the ID/EX operand path into the EX ALU and data-memory address cone. Prior attempts show that adding fetch prediction, extra address selectors, or a shared signed multiplier can easily cost more timing than they save, but the present ALU still instantiates signed/signed, unsigned/unsigned, and signed/unsigned multiply products on the same one-cycle result path used by hot ADD/address and low-half MUL operations. CoreMark benefits from one-cycle low MUL, while MULH/MULHU/MULHSU are expected to be very rare in the benchmark binary.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep ALU_MUL as the existing one-cycle unsigned low-half multiply, but remove real MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU hardware from rtl/alu.sv in normal synthesis. Add a small iterative high-multiply unit in EX that handles only MULH/MULHU/MULHSU, stalls the existing in-order pipeline through the same EX-stage long-latency mechanism used by DIV/REM, and writes the completed high half into EX/MEM when ready. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, preserve the current one-cycle algebraic substitutes so formal depth and the riscv-formal M-extension contract remain unchanged.\n\n  This targets a narrower cold cone than the failed shared-multiplier experiment: the common ADD/load-store/MUL path no longer pays signed high-product muxing or extra DSP routing, while CoreMark should keep the same cycle count unless it unexpectedly executes high-multiply instructions. The expected gain is primarily Fmax from a smaller ALU result mux and lower multiplier routing pressure, with limited IPC risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Keep one-cycle ALU_MUL low-half multiply, remove real MULH/MULHU/MULHSU products from the common combinational ALU path outside RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, and return zero for high-multiply ops that are intercepted in EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/iter_mulh.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact iterative high-multiply unit for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU with exact signed/unsigned RV32M semantics and a valid/consume handshake.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Detect high-multiply operations, launch the iterative unit, hold the EX payload while it runs, and capture the high-half result into EX/MEM using the existing long-latency stall style.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the EX-stage long-latency stall signal after extending it from DIV/REM-only to DIV/REM-or-high-MUL without changing top-level IO or the nret=1 RVFI contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Keep or extend focused MULH/MULHU/MULHSU edge vectors so the cold iterative unit is checked for signed, unsigned, mixed-sign, zero, and all-ones operands.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
