{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"micro_opt\\\") | \\\"\\\\nID: \\\\(.id)\\\\nTITLE: \\\\(.title)\\\\nOUTCOME: \\\\(.outcome) delta=\\\\(.delta_pct) fmax=\\\\(.fmax_mhz) lut4=\\\\(.lut4)\\\\nCP: \\\\(.critical_path.from) -> \\\\(.critical_path.to), cells=\\\\(.critical_path.logic_cells), levels=\\\\(.logic_levels), modules=\\\\(.critical_path.modules|join(\\\" > \\\"))\\\\nLESSON: \\\\(.lesson // \\\"\\\")\\\\nNOTES: \\\\(.implementation_notes // \\\"\\\" | gsub(\\\"\\\\n\\\"; \\\" \\\") | .[0:600])\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID: baseline-bench-b8d6a43\nTITLE: Baseline retest for cores/bench\nOUTCOME: improvement delta=0.0 fmax=5.442 lut4=12312\nCP: cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0 -> dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s, cells=156, levels=150, modules=clock_ibuf > cpu/u_fwd > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex\nLESSON: \nNOTES: \n\nID: hyp-20261004-001-r1s0\nTITLE: Iterative divide off ALU critical path\nOUTCOME: improvement delta=825.33 fmax=50.377 lut4=2674\nCP: cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0 -> dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s, cells=14, levels=14, modules=clock_ibuf > cpu/u_id > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex\nLESSON: - 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-001-r1s0 (improvement, +825.33%): Moving rare DIV/REM operations from the one-cycle ALU output mux into an EX-stage iterative unit can dramatically improve FPGA Fmax because CoreMark keeps the common ADD/address path hot while the deep divider cone mostly only taxes timing.\nNOTES: \n\nID: hyp-20261004-001-r2s0\nTITLE: Dedicated load-store address adder\nOUTCOME: regression delta=-10.3 fmax=45.189 lut4=2728\nCP: cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0 -> cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs1_val_27_s1, cells=42, levels=21, modules=clock_ibuf > cpu/u_id > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_if > cpu/u_hazard > cpu/u_id\nLESSON: - 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-001-r2s0 (regression, -10.30%): A dedicated LOAD/STORE address adder can regress CoreMark when it duplicates the same rs1+imm carry chain and adds EX result-select routing instead of removing the true regfile-to-dmem address bottleneck.\nNOTES: \n\nID: hyp-20261004-001-r3s0\nTITLE: Tighter load-use hazard gating\nOUTCOME: regression delta=2.55 fmax=51.654 lut4=2674\nCP: cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0 -> dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s, cells=13, levels=13, modules=clock_ibuf > cpu/u_id > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex\nLESSON: - 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-001-r3s0 (regression, +2.55%): Opcode-qualified load-use gating did not repay its added fetched-opcode decode and raw-imem comparator control, implying CoreMark's false immediate-bit load-use bubbles are rarer than the timing cost of making hazard detection more precise.\nNOTES: \n\nID: hyp-20261004-001-r4s0\nTITLE: Fast add-address execute path\nOUTCOME: regression delta=-7.43 fmax=46.636 lut4=2620\nCP: cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0 -> cpu/u_if/pc_13_s1, cells=41, levels=19, modules=clock_ibuf > cpu/u_id > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_if > cpu/u_hazard > cpu/u_id > cpu/u_if\nLESSON: - 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-001-r4s0 (regression, -7.43%): Splitting ADD/address into an EX fast path can still regress when `fast_result` control and an `ex_result` mux remain after the adder while the side ALU stays live, so avoiding post-adder selection on the rs1/imm-to-EX/MEM path matters more than just trimming the ALU case mux.\nNOTES: \n\nID: hyp-20261004-001-r5s0\nTITLE: Single shared multiplier datapath\nOUTCOME: regression delta=-3.76 fmax=48.481 lut4=2618\nCP: cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0 -> cpu/u_if/pc_27_s1, cells=52, levels=21, modules=clock_ibuf > cpu/u_fwd > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_if > cpu/u_hazard > cpu/u_id > cpu/u_if\nLESSON: - 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-001-r5s0 (regression, -3.76%): Sharing RV32M multiply variants through one `op`-selected 33x33 signed product can put sign-extension muxing and DSP mapping delay ahead of the hot one-cycle MUL path, outweighing reduced parallel-product area and ALU result mux fan-in.\nNOTES: \n\nID: hyp-20261004-001-r6s0\nTITLE: Iterative cold high-multiply unit\nOUTCOME: regression delta=-16.03 fmax=42.299 lut4=3187\nCP: cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s -> cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s100, cells=41, levels=22, modules=clock_ibuf > cpu/u_id > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_if > cpu/u_hazard > cpu/u_id\nLESSON: - 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-001-r6s0 (regression, -16.03%): Moving rare MULH/MULHU/MULHSU into an EX iterative unit can still lose when start/valid/stall control and EX/MEM capture muxing land on hot pipeline paths, outweighing removal of signed high-product hardware from the ALU.\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
