{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r7s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r7s0\ntitle: \"Sideband low dmem address path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current best core is Fmax-limited by paths that reach the data-memory\n  RAM address after passing through the forwarded operand and EX ALU cone.\n  Prior address-adder attempts regressed because they duplicated a full\n  effective-address adder and then added result-selection logic on the hot\n  EX/MEM path. The FPGA wrapper, however, indexes dmem only with\n  io_dmemAddr[12:2], while byte-lane selection and RVFI still need the full\n  architectural address to remain exact.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a narrow sideband effective-address calculation for memory operations:\n  compute rs1[12:0] + imm[12:0] in EX, carry those low address bits through\n  EX/MEM, and let MEM drive io_dmemAddr[12:2], byte masks, misalignment checks,\n  and load extraction from that sideband value. Keep the existing full\n  ALU result for architectural writeback, high address bits, MMIO marker\n  addresses, RVFI memory address reporting, and all non-memory operations.\n\n  This targets the current dmem-index timing cone without replaying stores,\n  altering the bus contract, or adding another selector after the full ALU\n  result. A 13-bit sideband adder should be cheaper and faster than the broad\n  RV32IM ALU/multiply result path for the only address bits that feed the\n  timed FPGA BRAM index, while preserving CoreMark cycle count and exact\n  RV32IM memory semantics.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a low-address sideband field to the EX/MEM payload for memory operations.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the EX/MEM payload sideband field for alphabetical build flows.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute and register the 13-bit low effective address from forwarded rs1 plus the immediate, without selecting it into the full ALU result.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the sideband low address bits for dmem_addr[12:2], byte masks, misalignment checks, load extraction, and RVFI aligned memory fields while preserving full high address bits from the existing ALU result.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
