{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r9s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r9s0\ntitle: \"Split redirect control fanout\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion has already removed the divider cone and preselected EX2 ALU operands, so its worst path has moved into the EX2 branch/redirect feedback path. The latest timing report starts at `ex1_q.rs2_val` and runs through `u_ex`, `u_if`, `u_id`, and finally the regfile control, which suggests the resolved branch comparator and single `redirect` signal are fanning into too much frontend combinational logic in the same cycle.\n\n  Prior predictor and fetch replay attempts lost because they added new PC-selection or instruction-decode work on this path. A narrower micro-optimization should keep the exact predict-not-taken behavior but reduce the amount of logic driven by the redirect decision.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the current monolithic EX redirect into separate registered-purpose control signals: one signal that only updates the IF PC to the resolved target, and a much narrower kill signal used by hazard/id_stage to clear valid bits in younger pipeline registers. Change IF output squashing so redirect does not force a full 32-bit NOP instruction through the decoder and regfile address path; instead, ID/EX is killed by valid/control clearing while the raw fetched instruction bits become irrelevant when valid is zero.\n\n  This preserves the existing branch penalty and RVFI ordering, but should shorten the `ex1_q.rs2_val` branch-compare-to-regfile-control cone by removing redirect from the fetched-instruction mux/decode/regfile-read address path. The intended implementation is deliberately small: no prediction, no new queues, and no LSU port reshaping.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Keep redirect priority for PC updates, but stop using redirect to mux the outgoing instruction to NOP; use only fetch-ready/flush valid control for frontend bubbles.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Treat invalid or flushed IF payloads as bubbles by clearing the ID/EX register control/valid fields, so wrong-path instruction bits do not matter and do not need to be decoded on redirect cycles.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Separate the EX resolved-PC update from younger-pipeline kill control, keeping redirect recovery precise while reducing broad redirect fanout through IF and ID combinational paths.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the split redirect/update and kill signals between EX, IF, ID, and hazard logic without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
