{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r10s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-002-r10s1\ntitle: \"Retimed divider postprocess stage\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's worst path has moved off the general ALU and into\n  `cpu/u_ex/u_divider`, specifically from divider state through the last\n  restoring divide step into `result_q`. That final cycle currently combines\n  remainder shift/compare/subtract, quotient-bit update, signed quotient or\n  remainder two's-complement correction, result selection, and the result\n  register load in one timed arc. CoreMark uses DIV/REM rarely enough that an\n  extra cycle on those operations is far cheaper than letting this cold unit\n  cap the whole FPGA clock.\nhypothesis: |\n  Restructure `iter_divider.sv` as a four-state divider with a separate\n  postprocess state after the 32nd restoring iteration. The run state should\n  register the final unsigned quotient and remainder as soon as the last bit is\n  computed, then a following postprocess cycle should apply signed correction\n  and choose quotient versus remainder before raising `valid`. Divide-by-zero\n  and signed-overflow special cases can keep their existing one-cycle fast\n  completion path.\n\n  This is a structural retime of the long-latency divider only: no new fetch,\n  prediction, LSU, or ALU muxing is introduced, and the existing EX-stage\n  `div_stall` handshake already tolerates one more non-special DIV/REM cycle.\n  The expected benefit is a shorter global Fmax limiter because the path from\n  `dividend_q`/`rem_q` to `result_q` is split across two registers, while\n  CoreMark IPC should barely move.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/iter_divider.sv\n    description: \"Add a registered final-quotient/remainder postprocess state that separates the last restoring divide iteration from signed result correction and quotient/remainder selection.\"\n  - file: test/test_iter_divider.py\n    description: \"Add focused divider latency and RV32M corner-case coverage for ordinary signed/unsigned DIV/REM plus divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 special cases.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
