{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r1s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-002-r1s1\ntitle: \"Move RV32M ops into a multi-cycle execute unit\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The baseline timing path is dominated by the EX-stage cone from forwarding\n  through the combinational ALU, and the current ALU computes multiply,\n  divide, and remainder hardware in the same always_comb block as every\n  single-cycle integer op. On Tang Nano 20K this creates a very deep LUT/DSP\n  path that caps Fmax around 5.4 MHz, far below the target and far more costly\n  than a few extra cycles on infrequent M-extension instructions.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split execute into a short single-cycle RV32I ALU/branch path plus a\n  dedicated multi-cycle RV32M unit. ADD/SUB/logic/shift/compare/address and\n  branch resolution continue to flow through the normal EX/MEM register, while\n  MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU/DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU start an M-unit transaction and hold\n  the front of the pipeline until the result is ready. MUL can use registered\n  DSP-friendly partial products or a small pipelined multiplier; DIV/REM should\n  use a 32-step iterative divider with signed pre/post processing for exact\n  RV32M semantics. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, keep the existing one-cycle\n  algebraic substitutes so the formal depth remains tractable. Removing\n  combinational multiply/divide/remainder from the always-active ALU should\n  collapse the worst path to forwarding plus a simple ALU/branch cone, giving a\n  large Fmax increase with limited CoreMark IPC loss.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 50\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Restrict the combinational ALU to RV32I single-cycle operations and ALTOPS-only M substitutes, so real multiply/divide/remainder hardware is no longer on the main EX path.\"\n  - file: rtl/m_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a dedicated RV32M execution unit with valid/busy/done handshake, registered multiplier path, iterative divider/remainder path, and exact RV32M corner-case handling.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Route decoded M-extension operations into the M unit, hold the EX payload while it is busy, and capture the completed result into EX/MEM without disturbing branch and memory behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add an EX-stage long-latency busy stall source so IF, ID, and EX/MEM are frozen consistently during multi-cycle M operations.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the new M-unit busy/done control between execute and hazard logic while preserving the single-retire RVFI interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Extend or adjust RV32M vectors to cover the new multi-cycle unit results, especially signed high-multiply and divide/remainder edge cases.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
