{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r2s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Retimed two-stage execute path\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion removed the divider from the one-cycle ALU, but the\n  reported worst path still runs through the register-file/forwarding path into\n  the execute ALU before reaching the next timed boundary. CoreMark is now more\n  likely limited by Fmax than by rare RV32M divide latency, so a structural\n  retiming of the hot execute cone is the most promising remaining angle in\n  this slot.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the existing EX stage into EX1 and EX2. EX1 performs operand selection,\n  MEM/WB and EX/MEM forwarding, branch compare input preparation, store-data\n  capture, and iterative-divider launch/hold bookkeeping, then registers the\n  selected operands, immediate, decoded control, and PC. EX2 contains the\n  actual RV32I ALU/address adder, one-cycle multiplier path, branch/jump target\n  calculation, misalignment checks, and the existing EX/MEM register update.\n\n  This adds one pipeline stage to the execute side and requires forwarding from\n  the new EX2/MEM boundary plus MEM/WB back to EX1, with load-use and\n  long-latency stalls updated accordingly. Taken branches and jumps gain one\n  cycle of penalty, but the dominant FPGA path should shrink from\n  regfile/forward muxes plus ALU/multiply output selection to one of those\n  halves. If Fmax rises by roughly 15-25%, the extra control-flow bubbles should\n  still clear the 4.6% acceptance threshold on CoreMark.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 12\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add an EX1/EX2 pipeline bundle carrying selected operands, store data, immediate, PC, decoded control, instruction, source/destination registers, and valid state.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the new EX1/EX2 bundle for alphabetical build flows that compile this shim before the real package file.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Retain the module boundary but internally split execute into an EX1 operand/forwarding register and an EX2 ALU/branch/memory-address register, preserving the existing iterative divider semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Retarget forwarding decisions to the new EX1 source stage, including bypasses from the EX2/MEM result and MEM/WB writeback result while avoiding invalid load data.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Update load-use, redirect, dmem, imem, and divider stall handling for the extra execute register so bubbles and holds remain precise.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the retimed execute-stage stall and forwarding interfaces without changing the top-level nret=1 RVFI or memory IO contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
