{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r10s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r10s2\ntitle: \"One-cycle lookahead BTB\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts found real CoreMark control-flow upside, but they lost\n  because table lookup, instruction decode, target addition, or return-stack\n  selection landed directly on the fetch PC-update path. The current champion's\n  timing is much healthier after the EX retimes, so the most promising remaining\n  predictor angle is to recover loop and direct-control bubbles while keeping\n  predictor SRAM/LUTRAM reads off the same-cycle PC path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny tagged BTB/BHT that is looked up one cycle ahead for the sequential\n  next fetch address rather than combinationally for the current PC. While the\n  core fetches PC N, a sideband lookup for PC N+4 is registered as the prediction\n  metadata that will be used if the next cycle really fetches N+4. The IF PC\n  update then chooses only between reset/EX repair, registered predicted target,\n  and fall-through PC+4; it does not perform a live table read, tag compare, or\n  immediate decode in the PC-update cone.\n\n  Train the table from the existing EX2 resolved control-flow metadata. Use a\n  small direct-mapped table, for example 16 or 32 entries with partial tags,\n  target PCs, and 2-bit counters. Conditional branches allocate/update only when\n  taken or already present, direct JALs allocate as always-taken targets, and\n  JALR can remain predict-not-taken unless a same-PC target proves stable. Carry\n  predicted_taken and predicted_target through ID/EX and EX1/EX2 so EX2 redirects\n  only on a mismatch between the registered prediction and the resolved next PC.\n  This should recover recurring CoreMark loop-back and direct-jump penalties with\n  much less Fmax risk than previous IF-side BHT/BTB/RAS predictors.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a small tagged BTB/BHT with EX training, one-cycle-ahead lookup for the next sequential PC, registered prediction outputs, and conservative update policy for conditional branches and direct jumps.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend IF/ID, ID/EX, and EX1/EX2 payloads with predicted_taken, predicted_target, and predicted_next_pc metadata needed for validation without re-reading predictor state in EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the prediction metadata fields in the alphabetical build-order shim.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use only registered predictor metadata in the PC update, issue sideband lookup requests for the next sequential PC, and invalidate the lookahead metadata on stalls and EX repair redirects.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch prediction metadata with the decoded instruction while preserving existing flush, stall, and bubble behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the carried prediction against the resolved branch or jump next PC, produce repair redirects only on mismatches, and emit compact predictor training information.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat prediction repair redirects like the current resolved redirect flush while keeping imem, dmem, divider, and RAW interlock precedence unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate the lookahead predictor, connect IF lookup and EX update paths, and preserve the nret=1 top-level IO and RVFI contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_lookahead_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused tests for taken loop prediction, loop exit repair, direct JAL prediction, stale lookahead invalidation across stalls, and redirect priority.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
