ractable. Removing\\ncombinational multiply/divide/remainder from the always-active ALU should\\ncollapse the worst path to forwarding plus a simple ALU/branch cone, giving a\\nlarge Fmax increase with limited CoreMark IPC loss.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 50, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\"\n…[134685 of 137757 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2e29420122766268]…\nta_pct\": -22.81, \"vs_baseline\": 763.45, \"fmax_mhz\": 51.261, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4898349, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3318, \"ff\": 982, \"seeds\": [48.875, 51.261, 51.261], \"perturbations\": [[0, 48.875, 19], [1, 51.261, 18], [2, 51.261, 18]], \"lutram\": 30, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/ex1_q.pc_2_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_1_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -15.461, \"arrival_ns\": 25.755, \"logic_cells\": 20, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_bp\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_id/u_decoder\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 19, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T04:42:34.074886Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-003-r10s2 (regression, -22.81%): One-cycle lookahead BTB reads still regressed because carrying `predicted_next_pc` metadata through IF/ID/EX and redirecting on an EX-wide resolved-next-PC compare adds enough control/register fanout that CoreMark loop-back wins do not repay it.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
