{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261004-003-r9s2\\\") | .hypothesis.hypothesis, .changes[]? | @text' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261004-003-r9s2\\\") | .hypothesis.hypothesis, .changes[]? | @text' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"Keep the frontend's prediction policy as static not-taken for conditional\nbranches, but register the taken-branch repair redirect for one cycle before\nit reaches IF and ID. Direct JAL and JALR should continue to redirect\nimmediately, because their targets do not depend on an rs1-vs-rs2 branch\ncompare and they are architecturally always taken. For conditional branches,\nEX2 still computes the branch condition and target in the normal place, but\nthe result only drives a small local kill for the younger instruction entering\nEX1; the PC update, IF flush, and ID flush consume a registered\nbranch_redirect_q on the next cycle.\n\nThis is effectively a static not-taken predictor with a retimed repair path:\ntaken conditional branches pay one extra recovery cycle, while not-taken\nbranches remain free and the hot EX compare no longer feeds the long\nEX-to-IF-to-ID/regfile combinational path reported by timing. If the removed\nfeedback lifts Fmax by more than the extra taken-loop penalty costs in\nCoreMark IPC, the net CoreMark iterations/second should clear the acceptance\nthreshold without adding any fetch-side tables, instruction decode, or target\nmuxes.\n\n{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Split resolved control outputs into immediate jump redirect and conditional branch redirect, keeping a local same-cycle younger-EX1 kill for taken conditional branches.\"}\n{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Register the conditional branch repair redirect for one cycle, combine it with immediate jump redirects for IF PC updates, and keep the nret=1 RVFI interface unchanged.\"}\n{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Separate local EX1 kill control from frontend redirect flush control so conditional branch compares no longer drive IF and ID in the same cycle.\"}\n{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Consume only the combined registered-branch-or-immediate-jump redirect path, preserving redirect priority over stalls and otherwise sequential fetch.\"}\n{\"file\":\"test/test_registered_branch_repair.py\",\"description\":\"Add focused cocotb coverage for taken conditional branch repair, not-taken fall-through, immediate JAL/JALR redirects, and dmem/imem stall interactions.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
