    description: \"Add an exact registered DIV/REM latency countdown predictor, drive div_stall from its active/done state, and capture divider results through the existing EX/MEM register when the predicted completion arrives.\"\n  - file: rtl/iter_divider.sv\n    description: \"Keep the divider result protocol intact but make its fixed latency explicit for the EX-stage predictor, with optional simulation assertions that predicted completion matches divider valid.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat the execute long-op stall input as registered predicted hold state so divider busy/valid no longer fans into IF, ID, and regfile read control.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the retimed divider hold signal without changing the nret=1 memory or RVFI interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_div_latency_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add directed DIV/REM tests for normal, divide-by-zero, signed-overflow, dependent-consumer, imem-stall, and dmem-stall cases to verify the predictor neither releases early nor double-retires.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
