{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r1s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Tiny BHT next-PC predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current pipeline always fetches pc+4 and resolves every taken branch or jump in EX, so tight CoreMark loops pay a two-instruction flush on each taken back edge. CoreMark's hot code has many direct loop branches and unconditional JAL control transfers whose targets are available from the fetched instruction bits, making them good candidates for a very small predictor that improves iterations per cycle without touching the memory contract.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small direct-branch next-PC predictor in IF: a 64-entry 2-bit saturating BHT indexed by pc[7:2], with direct JALs predicted taken immediately and conditional branches predicted taken only when the counter says taken and the instruction immediate supplies a valid aligned target. Carry predicted_taken and predicted_target through ID/EX, update the counter in EX from the actual branch result, and redirect only when the predicted next PC differs from the resolved next PC. This should remove most recurring loop-back flushes in CoreMark while adding only a modest LUT/FF footprint and no changes to RVFI retirement semantics.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a tiny 64-entry 2-bit BHT next-PC predictor for direct conditional branches, plus combinational JAL target prediction and EX-stage update inputs.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend IF/ID, ID/EX, and EX/MEM bundles with predicted next-PC metadata needed to validate or recover speculation at branch resolution.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the predictor's chosen next PC for fetch sequencing when not stalled, emit prediction metadata with the fetched instruction, and keep explicit redirect recovery highest priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch prediction metadata alongside the decoded instruction so EX can compare predicted and actual next PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve actual branch/jump next PC, flag mispredictions instead of all taken branches, and provide predictor update information for conditional branches.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate the predictor, wire IF prediction and EX update paths, and route pipeline flushes from misprediction recovery.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat EX misprediction recovery like the existing redirect flush while preserving current imem and dmem stall precedence.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
