{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"predictor|BHT|BTB|RAS|return|branch|next-PC|next PC|taken|flush|mispredict\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move RV32M ops into a multi-cycle execute unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline timing path is dominated by the EX-stage cone from forwarding\\nthrough the combinational ALU, and the current ALU computes multiply,\\ndivide, and remainder hardware in the same always_comb block as every\\nsingle-cycle integer op. On Tang Nano 20K this creates a very deep LUT/DSP\\npath that caps Fmax around 5.4 MHz, far below the target and far more costly\\nthan a few extra cycles on infrequent M-extension instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline timing path is dominated by the EX-stage cone from forwarding\\nthrough the combinational ALU, and the current ALU computes multiply,\\ndivide, and remainder hardware in the same always_comb block as every\\nsingle-cycle integer op. On Tang Nano 20K this creates a very deep LUT/DSP\\npath that caps Fmax around 5.4 MHz, far below the target and far more costly\\nthan a few extra cycles on infrequent M-extension instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split execute into a short single-cycle RV32I ALU/branch path plus a\\ndedicated multi-cycle RV32M unit. ADD/SUB/logic/shift/compare/address and\\nbranch resolution continue to flow through the normal EX/MEM register, while\\nMUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU/DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU start an M-unit transaction and hold\\nthe front of the pipeline until the result is ready. MUL can use registered\\nDSP-friendly partial products or a small pipelined multiplier; DIV/REM should\\nuse a 32-step iterative divider with signed pre/post processing for exact\\nRV32M semantics. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, keep the existing one-cycle\\nalgebraic substitutes so the formal depth remains tractable. Removing\\ncombinational multiply/divide/remainder from the always-active ALU should\\ncollapse the worst path to forwarding plus a simple ALU/branch cone, giving a\\nlarge Fmax increase with limited CoreMark IPC loss.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 50, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\"\n…[8005 of 11077 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6fb7fd88de930c2f]…\ngression\", \"fitness\": 12.56, \"delta_pct\": 3.63, \"vs_baseline\": 3.63, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.278, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4201766, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12748, \"ff\": 621, \"seeds\": [5.194, 5.278, 5.278], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.194, 145], [1, 5.278, 142], [2, 5.278, 142]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -187.524, \"arrival_ns\": 197.818, \"logic_cells\": 149, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 145, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T02:04:22.634690Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-003-r1s2 (regression, +3.63%): A tiny IF-side BHT/direct-JAL next-PC predictor can regress CoreMark when its `io_imemData` decode and target mux sit on the fetch PC-update path, because the added timing/metadata cost can outweigh recovered taken-back-edge flushes.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
