{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r2s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r2s2\ntitle: \"Tagged BTB without IF decode\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion still pays the full taken-control penalty because fetch\n  always advances to pc+4 and EX later redirects on taken branches and jumps.\n  The previous predictor attempt proved there is CoreMark cycle-count upside,\n  but it collapsed Fmax by decoding io_imemData and forming branch/JAL targets\n  directly in the fetch PC-update cone. A predictor that learns targets after\n  EX resolution and only indexes by PC in IF should recover hot loop and direct\n  jump penalties while staying off the existing forwarding/ALU critical path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny direct-mapped tagged branch target buffer, for example 16 or 32\n  entries, with valid, partial PC tag, target, and a 2-bit direction counter.\n  IF should consult it using only the current PC: on a tag hit with a taken\n  counter, next_pc becomes the stored target; otherwise next_pc remains pc+4.\n  EX resolves the real next PC as today, updates the entry for taken direct\n  branches/JAL/JALR and the saturating counter for conditional branches, and\n  redirects/flushed only when the predicted next PC differs from the actual\n  next PC. This deliberately avoids any io_imemData opcode/immediate decode in\n  IF, so the added timing is a small PC-indexed table read and mux rather than\n  an instruction-dependent target-generation path. Warm-up misses still behave\n  like the current core, while recurring CoreMark loop back edges and direct\n  jumps should retire with fewer bubbles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a small direct-mapped tagged BTB/BHT read by PC only, with EX-stage update ports for actual control-flow outcome and target.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry predicted-taken and predicted-next-PC metadata through IF/ID and ID/EX so EX can validate speculation.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the pipeline-bundle metadata additions for alphabetic build flows that compile this guarded shim first.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the BTB predicted next PC when present, keep redirect recovery highest priority, and avoid decoding io_imemData in the fetch path.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch prediction metadata with the decoded instruction without changing decode legality or RVFI data sources.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare predicted next PC against resolved next PC, emit redirects only on mismatch, and drive BTB update information from resolved control flow.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate and wire the predictor between IF and EX while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat prediction recovery like the existing redirect flush while preserving current imem, dmem, load-use, and divider stall behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
