{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r6s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r6s2\ntitle: \"Decode-stage static control predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current core still loses cycles on every taken direct branch and JAL\n  because fetch advances to pc+4 until EX resolves control flow. Prior\n  predictors recovered some CoreMark cycles but repeatedly lost more Fmax by\n  putting BHT/BTB/RAS lookup, tag compares, instruction predecode, or target\n  muxing directly in the IF next-PC path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a decode-stage static predictor for direct control flow instead of an\n  IF-side table predictor. When the instruction currently being decoded is a\n  direct JAL, or a conditional branch with a negative B-immediate, ID computes\n  the direct target using the existing decoded immediate path and asks IF to\n  update the PC to that target on the clock edge. This early redirect must not\n  squash the instruction currently in ID; it is a PC-only prediction path with\n  lower priority than real EX recovery and is gated off during imem, dmem,\n  load-use, or divider holds.\n\n  Carry compact prediction metadata through ID/EX so EX can validate the\n  static prediction. Correctly predicted JAL/backward taken branches retire\n  without the normal taken-redirect bubble; forward/not-taken branches behave\n  like the current core; loop exits recover by redirecting to pc+4 and\n  flushing the predicted-target instruction. This keeps all learned state out\n  of IF and avoids tag/counter/target-cache structures, while still attacking\n  the recurring CoreMark loop-back penalty that earlier predictor attempts\n  showed is worth several percent of IPC.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact predicted-taken and predicted-direct-control metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles, plus any precomputed direct-target field needed for EX validation.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the bundle metadata additions for alphabetic build flows that compile this guarded shim before core_pkg.sv.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute the static decode-stage prediction for direct JAL and negative-immediate conditional branches, latch its metadata, and expose a PC-only early-redirect request gated by valid unstalled decode.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Separate PC update redirection from instruction squashing so decode-stage predictions can steer the next fetch without replacing the current decoded instruction with a NOP; keep EX recovery redirect priority highest.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Validate the decode-stage prediction against the resolved branch or jump, suppress redirects for correct predictions, and redirect to the actual next PC on loop exits, aliases, JALR, or misalignment traps.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Gate decode-stage prediction during load-use, imem, dmem, and divider holds, and keep EX recovery flush behavior precise.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the decode-stage prediction request and metadata between ID, IF, EX, and hazard logic without changing the nret=1 top-level IO or RVFI contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
