{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r8s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r8s2\ntitle: \"IDEX early backedge predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion gained Fmax by splitting execute, but it now resolves\n  taken branches and jumps one stage later, so CoreMark loop backedges pay an\n  enlarged redirect penalty. Prior predictor attempts show that IF-side BHT,\n  BTB, RAS, decode feedback, and loop-replay machinery lose too much timing\n  when they decode io_imemData or select arbitrary learned targets on the\n  fetch PC path. A predictor that acts only from the already-registered ID/EX\n  branch metadata can recover part of the control penalty while keeping IF\n  nearly as simple as the champion.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a late static control predictor that fires when a valid ID/EX\n  instruction is actually allowed to enter EX1. For direct JAL, predict taken\n  to pc+imm. For conditional branches with a negative B-immediate, predict\n  taken to pc+imm; keep forward branches and JALR on the existing resolved\n  EX2 redirect path. Carry predicted_taken and predicted_target into the\n  EX1/EX2 payload. EX2 suppresses the normal redirect when the prediction\n  matches the resolved next PC, and redirects to the correct fall-through or\n  target on a mispredict.\n\n  This is intentionally weaker than a general BHT/BTB: it uses the decoded\n  control and immediate already sitting in ID/EX, adds no instruction-memory\n  decode, no tag table, and no multi-target lookup in IF. The only new PC\n  choice is an early redirect through the existing redirect-priority PC update\n  path, so Fmax risk should be much lower than the failed fetch predictors.\n  Hot CoreMark loops should save one redirect bubble per taken backedge, while\n  the occasional loop exit pays one corrective redirect.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend the EX1/EX2 payload with predicted_taken and predicted_target metadata for validation at branch resolution.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the new prediction metadata fields in the alphabetical typedef shim.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Generate a late static early-redirect prediction from valid ID/EX direct JALs and backward conditional branches that are advancing into EX1, latch prediction metadata, and convert EX2 control recovery from always-redirect-on-taken to redirect-on-mispredict.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Separate early predicted redirects from resolved EX2 redirects so early predictions flush younger IF/ID and ID/EX state without killing the branch just entering EX1, while resolved mispredicts still flush EX1.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire early predicted redirect and resolved mispredict redirect paths into the existing IF PC update and frontend flush controls without changing the nret=1 IO contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Accept the combined redirect target using the existing redirect-priority PC update path, with no instruction decode or table lookup added to IF.\"\n  - file: test/test_early_backedge_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for predicted taken backward loops, loop-exit mispredict recovery, direct JAL prediction, JALR fallback, and stall interactions.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
