able. Removing\\ncombinational multiply/divide/remainder from the always-active ALU should\\ncollapse the worst path to forwarding plus a simple ALU/branch cone, giving a\\nlarge Fmax increase with limited CoreMark IPC loss.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 50, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\"\n…[116453 of 119525 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1a209d2e4f845a6f]…\n, \"delta_pct\": -15.61, \"vs_baseline\": 736.39, \"fmax_mhz\": 53.399, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 5267491, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2907, \"ff\": 751, \"seeds\": [50.655, 53.399, 53.399], \"perturbations\": [[0, 50.655, 24], [1, 53.399, 24], [2, 53.399, 24]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/ex1_q.rs2_val_2_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_ER_s195\", \"slack_ns\": -14.742, \"arrival_ns\": 25.036, \"logic_cells\": 74, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_rf\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 24, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T04:15:01.842558Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-003-r8s2 (regression, -15.61%): ID/EX-only backedge prediction still regressed because `early_redirect` feedback into the global PC/hazard path plus EX2 `resolved_next_pc` versus `predicted_next_pc` validation costs more than CoreMark recovers from one-stage-earlier loop redirects.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
