{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The existing stall is the blunt one: any memory op in EX/MEM plus `!io_dmemReady` freezes the pipe. I’m replacing that with MEM-owned “can this request retire?” signals so ordinary RAM stores can commit into a single registered write request while the slot drains."}}
